# Frontend Zero-Bloat Protocol

## 1. DESIGN.md Token Enforcement
- **Mandatory Pre-Read:** Before writing or modifying any Tailwind utility classes or CSS rules, read `DESIGN.md` in the project root.
- **Strict Token Usage:** Use ONLY the spacing, typography, color variables, border radii, and breakpoints defined in `DESIGN.md`.
- **Ban Arbitrary Values:** Do NOT invent arbitrary Tailwind values (e.g., `w-[347px]`, `bg-[#1a2b3c]`) or inline styles unless explicitly specified in `DESIGN.md`.

## 2. Component Discipline
- Keep components flat and single-purpose. Avoid deep prop-drilling or premature wrapper components.
- Co-locate local state where it is consumed; lift state only when shared by direct siblings.
- Reuse existing UI primitives before creating new elements.
